## Pipeline Variants

The router (`steps/route.md`) selects a variant based on project state and
user input. Each variant composes a different step sequence.

### Decision tree

```
Is there a planned sprint with stories ready for implementation?
  YES --> sprint-execute
  NO  |
      v
Is this a bug fix?
  YES --> bug
  NO  |
      v
Is this carry-over / next sprint work?
  YES --> carry-over
  NO  |
      v
Is this analysis-only (no implementation requested)?
  YES --> analysis-only
  NO  |
      v
Do trusted planning artifacts exist on disk?
  (product brief AND prd AND architecture)
  YES --> feature
  NO  |
      v
Do ANY planning artifacts exist?
  YES --> Are they trusted / current?
    NOT SURE --> brownfield-c
    NO, STALE --> Is code mid-implementation?
      YES --> brownfield-a
      NO  --> brownfield-b
  NO  --> Is there an existing codebase with source files?
    YES --> brownfield-b
    NO  --> greenfield
```

### Variant pipeline sequences

| Variant | Step Sequence |
|---------|--------------|
| **sprint-execute** | implementation --> sprint-review --> deploy-validate --> retro |
| **greenfield** | discovery --> research-requirements --> architecture --> stories-test-strategy --> [ui-direction] --> implementation --> sprint-review --> deploy-validate --> retro |
| **feature** | discovery --> research-requirements --> architecture --> stories-test-strategy --> [ui-direction] --> implementation --> sprint-review --> deploy-validate --> retro |
| **bug** | bug-investigation --> implementation --> deploy-validate --> retro |
| **carry-over** | carry-over-evaluation --> discovery --> research-requirements --> architecture --> stories-test-strategy --> [ui-direction] --> implementation --> sprint-review --> deploy-validate --> retro |
| **brownfield-a** | codebase-inventory --> discovery --> research-requirements --> architecture --> stories-test-strategy --> implementation --> sprint-review --> deploy-validate --> retro |
| **brownfield-b** | deep-codebase-analysis --> discovery --> research-requirements --> architecture --> stories-test-strategy --> [ui-direction] --> implementation --> sprint-review --> deploy-validate --> retro |
| **brownfield-c** | doc-reconciliation --> doc-repair-backfill --> discovery --> research-requirements --> architecture --> stories-test-strategy --> [ui-direction] --> implementation --> sprint-review --> deploy-validate --> retro |
| **analysis-only** | deep-codebase-analysis --> STOP |

`[ui-direction]` is conditional -- included only when sprint stories
introduce new visual surfaces (new UI components, pages, or layout changes).
This is determined during the stories-test-strategy step, not by the router.

