/bmad-validate-prd         -- PRD completeness check
/bmad-create-architecture  -- Phase 2 system design
/bmad-check-implementation-readiness -- PRD/arch completeness for stories
/bmad-create-epics-and-stories  -- Phase 2 story breakdown
/bmad-sprint-planning      -- Phase 2 sprint selection
```

### Quality and Validation
```
/bmad-party-mode                   -- multi-agent debate
/bmad-review-adversarial-general   -- cynical review, ONE-SHOT only
/bmad-advanced-elicitation         -- probe until zero ambiguity
/bmad-agent-tea-tea                -- TEA test strategy
```

The Rule 8 **convergence cycle** (run until zero CRITICAL/MAJOR) is NOT a skill:
the lead dispatches the `adversary` role, which runs the native method in
`team-roles/adversary.md` and stamps `skill: ai-dlc-adversary-review`. The bmad
review skill above is for ONE-SHOT sweeps (`bug-investigation`, `sprint-review`,
test strategy) — its "find ≥10, HALT on zero, no severity" contract has no fixed
point in a loop that must reach zero.

### Implementation
```
/bmad-create-story         -- create a single story
/bmad-dev-story            -- implement a single story
/bmad-code-review          -- validate implementation quality
/bmad-correct-course       -- remediation when validation fails
```
